  "prospective_policies": [
    "The implemented protocol is named pinned_generic_script_defaults_not_journal_reconstruction. Reject configurations that differ; do not infer a journal reference from generic defaults.",
    "Exact declared cell roster, full 201 pseudo identities (-1 real and 1..200 null), ten repeats, and actual 50-fold partitions are required. The exported n_folds scalar is not trusted.",
    "Targets, prediction payload, input-object manifest and exposure policy use explicit SHA-256. Digests bind submitted evidence; they do not establish truthful execution or independent freezing.",
    "One single Beryl region per cell; all probes merged per source session. No composite regions, widefield export or silent complete-case selection.",
    "Real and pseudo masks must retain the same ordered trial identities for this component; variable masks are rejected pending explicit source mapping.",
    "Constant targets and nonfinite inputs are rejected, rather than accepting sklearn force_finite substitutions.",
    "Movement pairs require all seven source predictors and identical actual trial IDs/targets. Null identities are not assumed exchangeable across regions and motor. Paired R2 differences are descriptive, not the source in-sample motor-residual analysis.",
    "Fisher/BH follows source session-level inference and does not provide mouse-clustered uncertainty or held-out animal generalization."
  ],
